)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Initiator Panel                          !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}  The Initiator panel (INIT) lists the JES2 initiators. SDSF asks JES2
}  each time ($DI) and reads the answer from the system log. INIT takes
}  no parameters; it needs READ access to SDSF.OPER.
}
{  ID       }The initiator's number.
{  STATUS   }INACTIVE, ACTIVE, DRAINED, HALTED, ... as JES2 gives it.
{  CLASSES  }The job classes it selects, in that order. Overtype them to
}            change them ($TI); JES2 keeps five at most.
{  JOB-NAME, STEP-NAME, PROC-STEP, TYPE, JNUM, C, ASID }
}            The job an active initiator runs.
}  Active initiators are white, the others blue.
}
}  Action characters:
{   D  }Display the initiator ($DI).
{   S  }Start it ($SI).
{   P  }Stop it once its job has ended ($PI).
{   Z  }Halt it: it takes no new job until S ($ZI).
}  D needs READ access to SDSF.OPER, the others UPDATE access; without
}  it: NOT AUTHORIZED FOR INIT. JES2's answers go to the system log.
}
}
}  Enter: next topic   PF7: contents   PF10: back   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFHLSM
  &ZUP = ISFHTOC
)END
